# Review: BlueskyPlugin

Most of the spec is implemented, but nothing is tested: the package has no `*.test.ts` file, and its
one story covers the read-only channel backend, not sync. Target discovery, the page walk with cursor
stop, the page budgets and hard cap, PDS resolution for `did:plc` and `did:web`, and the Edge
`/atproto/proxy` path all match the spec in code.

The spec still describes the older `Integration.targets` model. The code runs on plugin-connector
bindings: `Binding.syncAll` fans out over `Cursor` objects, the remote id is `spec.externalId`, the
last seen URI is `cursor.max`, and errors go to `cursor.lastError`. The biggest behavioural
divergence is F-4.2: the `Subscription.Feed` is created eagerly by a third operation,
`MaterializeBlueskyTarget`, when a binding is made. Sync never creates it, and it skips a binding
whose target is not a feed. Two more gaps matter. First, `runRequest` never filters non-2xx
statuses, so an XRPC JSON error body fails schema decoding and is not retried, which leaves F-6.4
unmet in practice. Second, `GetBlueskyTargets` swallows the missing-handle and PDS errors into its
best-effort fallback instead of raising them.

Of 51 items: 0 done, 34 untested, 3 partial, 3 diverged, 11 missing (all ten scenarios and QA-1).

