```mdl
verdict SyncBlueskyTargets: Pull-syncs every binding of the connection and returns the appended total; the feed is not created here.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/definitions.ts#SyncBlueskyTargets, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/sync.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/materialize-target.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The definition takes a connection ref and optional priority and returns appended. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/definitions.ts#SyncBlueskyTargets
    - The handler fans out over the connection's cursors with Binding.syncAll and syncs each through the credentials layer. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/sync.ts
    - MaterializeBlueskyTarget creates the Subscription.Feed when a binding is made, before any sync. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/operations/materialize-target.ts
  note: |
    The page walk, cursor stop, budgets and per-binding error recording match. The difference is the first sync: the
    spec says sync materializes the feed and pins it to `target.object`, but sync only loads `binding.spec.target`
    and skips the binding if it is not a `Subscription.Feed`. No test.
```

