```mdl
verdict F-6.4: Retry is exponential with jitter, but HTTP status errors are never raised, so 429/5xx are not retried.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/services/BlueskyApi.ts#runRequest, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/services/BlueskyApi.ts#shouldRetry]
  note: |
    `runRequest` calls `httpClient.execute` without `HttpClient.filterStatusOk`, so a 429 or 5xx response goes to
    `res.json` and schema decode; a JSON error body then fails as `SchemaError`, which `shouldRetry` rejects. The
    `StatusCodeError` branch is unreachable. `Schedule.upTo({ times: 3 })` also allows 3 retries (4 attempts), not 3
    attempts. No test.
```

```mdl
verdict F-6.5: Schema errors are not retried, but non-JSON error bodies surface as transport errors and are retried.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bluesky/src/services/BlueskyApi.ts#shouldRetry]
  note: |
    With no status filter, a 4xx with a JSON body fails decode and is not retried (as intended), but a 4xx with a
    non-JSON body fails in `res.json` as an `HttpClientError` whose reason is not `StatusCodeError`, so it is retried.
    No test.
```

